component SigilDesignInput {
  goal {
    Preserve resolved authored language structure at the TypeScript to sigilc
    boundary without precomputing semantic meaning.
  }

  interface {
    ResolvedDesignInput {
      Load the workspace through its parser and resolver. Return frontend schema 2
      with explicit languageVersion 0.8.0 separate from the frontend artifact
      version, exact source/context buffers, diagnostics, components, Facets, Tag
      introductions and grouping occurrences, explicit import selections, bare
      references, and Inline Links.

      Record config and glossary buffers used during loading, including absent
      optional inputs. Rust validates current bytes and owns their fingerprints. Keep
      Facets attributed to their physical file, canonical component owner, and
      contract role. Preserve units even when owner resolution fails, alongside
      diagnostics. Export this capability from the core language package. Keep no
      forwarding export or compatibility helper in the removed TypeScript compiler
      package.
    }
  }

  constraints {

    SourceFidelity {
      Preserve exact Tag names and owner identity, selection provenance, link labels,
      targets and ranges, optional grouping identity, and all references per Facet;
      no exported visibility, expand form, or single-Concept field remains.

      Invalid UTF-8 returns a language failure with diagnostics and no purportedly
      faithful JSON bundle. Other language failures retain structurally representable
      partial results and diagnostics; native consumers never treat them as
      successful compilation.
    }
    StructuralBoundary {
      The bundle contains no Turtle, semantic laws, inferred relationships,
      obligations, implementation requirements, ranking, or semantic verdicts.
      Imports provide language visibility, never automatic runtime dependencies.
      Source ranges identify authored units, not evidence of implementation. Input
      capture invokes no model and selects no external workflow.
    }
  }

  cases {
    PhysicalInventory {
      Multiple components or Facets produce source inventories with exact owners and
      physical ranges. Prose, Inline Links, and fenced payloads remain in captured
      source even when no model interprets them.
    }

    SourceCapture {
      A config or source changing after loading cannot change the captured bundle.
      Rust rejects publication against mismatching current inputs.
    }
  }
}
